Description: SuperMox Manager - desktop app for a SuperMox cluster
 A GTK 3 window that shows the PVE web interface of one node of a SuperMox
 cluster, so you can manage the cluster from the desktop instead of from a
 terminal. The window chrome is SuperMox's: a node picker in the header bar
 picks which node to talk to, and the app trusts exactly that node's TLS
 certificate (its fingerprint comes from the signed membership list, or from
 the node's own certificate file when the node is this one) and nothing else.
 There is no "accept an unsafe certificate" prompt anywhere in the app.
 .
 Everything inside the window is the PVE web interface, so the user you see
 is the user PAM decides, and the actions available are the ones that user
 may perform. The app keeps nothing on disk except the window size and the
 last node you picked.
 .
 Run it as "supermox-manager"; it opens https://127.0.0.1:8006/ for the local
 node and https://<host>:8006/ for a remote one.
